/* Auto-generated by scripts/build-user-guide-search.js — do not edit by hand. */
window.DOCS_SEARCH_INDEX = [{"file":"getting-started.html","title":"Getting Started","sections":[{"t":"Getting Started","b":"Create your account, connect your first channel and send your first message — in about 15 minutes."},{"t":"Getting Started — 1. Create your account","b":"1 Open the sign-up page and enter your name, email and a strong password . 2 Check your inbox for the verification email and click the verification link. Didn't get it? Check spam, then use Resend verification on the login screen. 3 Log in with your new credentials. If two-factor authentication is enabled for your account, enter the code from your authenticator app. 💡 Tip You can also sign in with a magic link — request it from the login page and click the link we email you, no password needed."},{"t":"Getting Started — 2. Complete the onboarding wizard","b":"After your first login, the onboarding wizard guides you through the essentials. It tracks seven steps: Step What to do Verify email Confirm your email address (automatic once you click the link). Choose a plan Pick a subscription that matches your team size and volume. Connect first channel Link WhatsApp (Cloud API or QR), Messenger or Instagram. Import first contacts Add contacts manually or import from a CSV/Excel file. Send first message Use a campaign or the inbox to start a conversation. Train first chatbot Create an AI chatbot and attach a knowledge base. Connect social account Link Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn or X for posting. Each step links directly to the right page, and you can mark steps complete yourself if you've already done them elsewhere. Once all steps are done the wizard disappears from your dashboard."},{"t":"Getting Started — 3. Dashboard tour","b":"The dashboard is your mission control. What you see here: Stat cards — conversations, contacts, campaign activity and AI usage at a glance. Charts — message volume and social posting trends over time. Quick links — jump straight to the Inbox, Campaigns or Automations. Onboarding widget — visible until you complete all setup steps. 📷 Screenshot placeholder: client dashboard overview"},{"t":"Getting Started — 4. Workspaces","b":"A workspace is a separate container for one business, brand or client. Contacts, conversations, campaigns, chatbots and settings are all scoped to a workspace — nothing is shared between them. Go to Account → Workspaces to create additional workspaces (if your plan allows). Switch between workspaces from the workspace switcher at the top of the sidebar. Each workspace has its own channels, so you can run multiple brands from one login."},{"t":"Getting Started — 5. Profile & preferences","b":"1 Click your avatar (bottom of the sidebar) and open Settings . 2 Update your name, email and password , and upload a profile photo. 3 Choose your language and currency — the entire interface translates instantly. 4 Pick light or dark theme under Theme. The app follows your choice on every device you log in from."},{"t":"Getting Started — Next steps","b":"Connect your first channel — start with WhatsApp . Set up your first AI chatbot . Send a broadcast campaign to your contacts."}]},{"file":"inbox.html","title":"Unified Inbox","sections":[{"t":"Unified Inbox","b":"One shared inbox for WhatsApp, Messenger and Instagram — so your team never misses a conversation, no matter where it started."},{"t":"Unified Inbox — Inbox layout","b":"The inbox has three panels: Left — conversation list. Every conversation with unread badge, last message preview and channel icon. Use the search box and status filters (Open / Pending / Resolved) to find things fast. Middle — conversation thread. The full message history, including media, voice notes, quoted replies and template messages. Right — contact details. Customer profile, tags, and contact fields. Click the name to open the full contact record. 📷 Screenshot placeholder: inbox with a conversation open"},{"t":"Unified Inbox — Supported channels","b":"Channel How it connects Guide WhatsApp Cloud API Official Meta connection with your business number WhatsApp guide WhatsApp QR Scan a QR code with WhatsApp (co-existence mode) WhatsApp guide Messenger Facebook login via embedded signup Channel setup Instagram Instagram business login Instagram guide Connect or disconnect channels any time from Inbox → Channel Setup . Channel counts may be limited by your subscription plan."},{"t":"Unified Inbox — Replying to messages","b":"1 Select a conversation from the list. 2 Type your reply in the composer at the bottom. Press Enter to send, Shift+Enter for a new line. 3 Use the toolbar above the composer to attach images, videos, documents or record a voice note with the mic button. You can also hover any earlier message and use the reply action — your answer appears as a quoted reply, just like in WhatsApp. 💡 Canned replies Save your team's common answers under Inbox → Canned Replies . While typing, insert one and edit before sending — perfect for greetings, pricing answers and support hours."},{"t":"Unified Inbox — Voice notes","b":"Click the mic button in the composer to start recording; the timer shows elapsed seconds. Stop to preview the recording, then send — WhatsApp voice notes play natively on the customer's phone. Your browser will ask for microphone permission the first time — click Allow. 📎 Instagram audio Instagram voice notes are delivered as standard audio bubbles (Meta doesn't support WhatsApp's voice-note bubble), but recording and sending works the same way."},{"t":"Unified Inbox — Labels","b":"Labels are coloured tags for conversations — for example Urgent , Awaiting Payment or VIP . 1 Create your team's labels under Inbox → Labels (choose name and colour). 2 In a conversation, open the label picker and attach any labels. 3 Filter the conversation list by label to work through a queue — for example everything tagged Awaiting Payment . 🤖 Automatic label When the AI chatbot hands a chat over to a human, an amber “Waiting for you” label is attached automatically and removed once an agent replies."},{"t":"Unified Inbox — Team assignment","b":"Assign a conversation to a teammate from the conversation header — they'll see it in their own queue. Change the status: Open (needs action), Pending (waiting on customer) or Resolved (done). Everyone sees the same inbox in real time — new messages appear without refreshing."},{"t":"Unified Inbox — When the AI hands over","b":"If your chatbot is answering and a customer asks for a human: The bot immediately tells the customer an agent is joining (you can customise this message per chatbot). The conversation gets the “Waiting for you” label and stays on top of your queue. The bot stays silent after handover — the human agent owns the thread."},{"t":"Unified Inbox — The 24-hour window (WhatsApp & Instagram)","b":"Meta rules: free-form replies are only allowed within 24 hours of the customer's last message. Outside that window: WhatsApp: send an approved template message to re-open the conversation. Instagram: after the window closes, messages can still be sent with the human-agent tag for up to 7 days. ⚠️ Plan ahead Set up an automation or a follow-up campaign instead of replying manually outside the window."}]},{"file":"whatsapp.html","title":"WhatsApp","sections":[{"t":"WhatsApp","b":"Connect your WhatsApp Business number, manage message templates, automate replies and add WhatsApp chat to your website."},{"t":"WhatsApp — Connecting WhatsApp","b":"Go to Inbox → Channel Setup . Two connection types are available — pick based on how your number is set up: Cloud API (official) QR session Best for Businesses wanting the official Meta API Quick start with your existing WhatsApp number Setup Meta business verification, one-click embedded signup Scan a QR code from WhatsApp → Linked Devices Campaigns Full template broadcast support Depends on your session type Stability Highest — backed by Meta Runs alongside your phone app 1 Click Connect WhatsApp (Cloud API) or Connect WhatsApp QR . 2 For QR: open WhatsApp on your phone → Settings → Linked Devices → Link a Device → scan the code shown. Keep your phone online until the session syncs. 3 For Cloud API: follow the Meta embedded-signup popup — log in to Facebook, pick your business and number, and approve permissions. The webhook is registered automatically. 4 The channel appears in your inbox — new customer messages start arriving automatically. ⚠️ QR sessions A QR session runs through your own number and can disconnect if the phone is offline for long or the device is removed. Re-scan from the channel page if the status shows disconnected."},{"t":"WhatsApp — Message templates","b":"Templates are pre-approved message formats you can send outside the 24-hour reply window — for order updates, offers and reminders. 1 Open Messaging → Templates and click New Template . 2 Choose a category (Marketing, Utility or Authentication) and write the body. Add variables like {{1}} for personalisation — e.g. “Hi {{1}}, your order {{2}} has shipped!”. 3 Submit for approval. Meta usually reviews within minutes to a few hours. Status shows under Templates. 4 Once approved, use the template in the inbox, in campaigns and in automations . 💡 Approval tips Be specific and honest with the category, avoid aggressive ALL-CAPS promotions, and use a clear footer with an opt-out line (e.g. “Reply STOP to unsubscribe”)."},{"t":"WhatsApp — Auto-replies","b":"Auto-replies answer incoming messages instantly based on keywords — great for FAQs and after-hours responses. 1 Open Messaging → Auto-Replies and click New . 2 Enter trigger keywords (e.g. “price, rates, cost”) and the reply text. Matching is not case-sensitive. 3 Toggle the auto-reply active . It fires on every matching inbound message on the connected number. 📎 Good to know When a customer explicitly asks for a human, the chatbot stops and hands over — auto-replies and bots never trap a customer in a loop."},{"t":"WhatsApp — Website chat widget","b":"Turn website visitors into WhatsApp conversations with an embeddable chat bubble. 1 Open Messaging → Chat Widget and customise the bubble: colour, greeting text, position and your brand avatar. 2 Copy the generated embed snippet . 3 Paste it just before </body> on your website (or send it to your developer). The bubble appears on your site immediately."},{"t":"WhatsApp — Quality & limits","b":"Messaging limits (how many unique customers you can message per day) grow automatically as Meta observes quality traffic. Keep opt-outs honoured, avoid spammy blasts, and monitor template quality — a low-quality rating slows your sending. Check Reports → Campaigns to watch delivery and read rates per broadcast."}]},{"file":"instagram.html","title":"Instagram","sections":[{"t":"Instagram","b":"Turn Instagram comments into DM conversations, guide followers through multi-step flows and reply with rich carousels."},{"t":"Instagram — Connecting Instagram","b":"1 Go to Inbox → Channel Setup and click Connect Instagram . 2 Log in with your Instagram professional (business or creator) account and approve the requested permissions. 3 DMs and comment events arrive in your inbox automatically — the webhook registers itself on first connect, no manual Meta setup needed. ⚠️ Professional account required Personal Instagram accounts can't connect. Switch to a Business or Creator account in the Instagram app first (it's free)."},{"t":"Instagram — Comment automations","b":"A comment automation watches your posts and replies to commenters — typically sending them a DM. The classic funnel: comment a keyword → get a DM → unlock a link or content . 1 Open Instagram → Automations and click New Automation . 2 Choose the post or reel to monitor and the keyword that triggers it (e.g. “comment LINK”). 3 Pick what happens next: send a DM message or run a DM flow . Optionally ask the commenter to follow you before unlocking content. 4 Activate it. Every matching comment gets a reply and/or DM automatically. 💡 Funnel logs Open Instagram → Funnel Logs to see every comment, whether it matched, and what was sent — perfect for checking that your funnel works."},{"t":"Instagram — DM flows (multi-step)","b":"DM flows are visual, multi-step conversations: welcome message, buttons, questions and answers — like a mini chatbot inside Instagram DMs. Create flows under Instagram → DM Flows with the visual builder. Add steps: text messages, button choices, and questions that save the answer (name, email, preference…). Attach a flow from any comment automation, or start one from the inbox. The follow ask on step 2 works with the uncapped-gate loop: followers skip ahead, non-followers get a friendly follow prompt first."},{"t":"Instagram — Templates (carousels & buttons)","b":"Rich Instagram DMs are built from templates in the Instagram → Templates gallery: Button templates — a message with up to three tappable buttons (open URL, next step). Carousel templates — swipeable product cards with image, title and buttons each. Compose with the live customer-view preview , then send from the inbox or attach to automations and flows. 📷 Screenshot placeholder: Instagram template gallery with carousel editor"},{"t":"Instagram — Good to know","b":"DMs are possible only with people who message you first or comment — Instagram doesn't allow cold DMs. Media (photos, audio, video) can be sent in DMs; files are delivered through a public URL that Meta fetches. Outside the 24-hour window, replies use the human-agent tag for up to 7 days after the customer's last message."}]},{"file":"ai-chatbots.html","title":"AI & Chatbots","sections":[{"t":"AI & Chatbots","b":"Let AI answer your customers 24/7 — trained on your own content, with smooth human handover when it's needed."},{"t":"AI & Chatbots — AI providers","b":"Chatbots need an AI engine behind them. Under AI → Providers you connect a provider account and choose the models used for chat and embeddings (used for knowledge-base search). 1 Open AI → Providers and click Add Provider . 2 Pick a provider (for example OpenAI or Google Gemini) and paste your API key . 3 Set the chat model — auto is recommended; the platform then routes to the best healthy model automatically. 4 Enable it and run the built-in diagnostic to confirm everything is wired correctly. 📎 Keep a fallback Add at least one embed-capable provider. Without embeddings your chatbot falls back to keyword search only, which can miss answers."},{"t":"AI & Chatbots — Knowledge bases","b":"A knowledge base (KB) is your bot's brain: paste or upload your content and the bot answers from it instead of making things up. 1 Create a KB under AI → Knowledge Bases (name it after its purpose, e.g. “Store FAQ”). 2 Add documents : paste text, upload files, or import FAQ/question-answer content. Every document is automatically split into chunks and indexed. 3 After editing a document, re-index it (re-save or use the re-index action) so the search index refreshes. 💡 What makes a good KB Write the way customers ask: short Q&A pairs, product names spelled out, prices, policies, opening hours. The bot can only answer what's actually in the KB — generic company questions need the company info written there too."},{"t":"AI & Chatbots — Creating a chatbot","b":"1 Open AI → Chatbots and click New Chatbot . 2 Give it a name and a system prompt — its personality and rules, e.g. “You are the assistant for X Store. Be friendly, answer in the customer's language, only promise what's in the knowledge base.” 3 Attach a knowledge base — this is what grounds its answers in your content. 4 Set the handover reply — the message sent when a customer asks for a human (translated into 17 languages automatically if left empty). 5 Activate the chatbot. It now answers inbound messages on the channels it's attached to."},{"t":"AI & Chatbots — Memories","b":"AI → Memories shows what the bot has learned about individual customers — preferences and facts it picked up from conversations. Use it to review what the AI remembers and remove anything that shouldn't be stored."},{"t":"AI & Chatbots — Testing in the playground","b":"Every chatbot has a playground — a private chat where you test before going live: Ask questions your customers would ask and check the answers. The playground remembers the conversation, so follow-up questions work like a real chat. Try edge cases: a question not in the KB, a request for a human, an angry message with emojis. 💡 Bot ignoring your KB? Test with a question that literally appears in your KB text. If the playground still answers poorly, re-index your documents and run the provider diagnostic — the usual culprits are a missing embed provider or an unindexed document."},{"t":"AI & Chatbots — Human handover","b":"When a customer says “talk to a human” (or the AI detects strong frustration): The bot instantly acknowledges with your handover message. The conversation is labelled “Waiting for you” in the inbox. The bot goes quiet — a human agent takes over and the label clears on the first agent reply. You can also hand over manually from any automation with the Assign agent node, or from the inbox."},{"t":"AI & Chatbots — Monitoring AI usage","b":"Open Reports → AI to see chatbot activity and usage over time — helpful for understanding volume and spotting cost spikes. See the Reports guide ."}]},{"file":"automations.html","title":"Automations","sections":[{"t":"Automations","b":"Visual flow builder that reacts to events — welcome new contacts, recover carts, route leads and let AI answer — all without code."},{"t":"Automations — The builder","b":"Open Automations from the sidebar and create a new automation. The builder is a canvas: drag nodes from the left palette, connect them into a flow, and configure each node in its panel. Every automation has exactly one trigger (the entry event) followed by any sequence of action nodes. Templates — start from ready-made recipes instead of a blank canvas. Test — dry-run your flow before activating; nothing is sent and no tags are applied. Status — automations only fire while active ; pausing stops all runs instantly."},{"t":"Automations — Triggers (when a flow starts)","b":"Trigger Fires when… Great for New contact a contact is created (message, import, form…) Welcome messages & onboarding Tag added any tag is attached to a contact VIP treatment, import follow-ups Message received a customer messages you (optional keyword filter) Keyword menus, AI receptionist Campaign sent a campaign message is delivered (per recipient) Post-campaign follow-ups Form submitted a WhatsApp flow/form is completed Bookings, lead capture, surveys Webhook received an external system POSTs to your flow's URL Payment alerts, CRM sync Order placed a store order comes in Order confirmations Order fulfilled an order is shipped/completed Tracking + delivery feedback Order cancelled an order is cancelled Win-back offers, feedback Cart abandoned a cart is left without checkout Cart recovery sequences New customer a store customer record is created Welcome coupons 💡 Keyword filter On Message received , leave keywords empty to run on every message, or list comma-separated keywords (e.g. menu, price, rates ) to run only when one appears in the message."},{"t":"Automations — What nodes can do","b":"Category Nodes Send WhatsApp text, message template, media, quick-reply buttons, list messages, SMS, email, sequences Listen Ask a question and store the customer's next reply Logic Condition (branch the flow), Wait (delay minutes to days), Webhook call, Run sub-flow AI AI reply — let your chatbot compose the answer Contact Add/remove tag, update contact fields, assign to agent, add to campaign Engage CTA button, location, poll, run chatbot, book appointment, Google Meet, WhatsApp form Commerce WhatsApp catalog, WooCommerce & Shopify product pickers Integrations Google Sheets, Google Docs, Google Forms"},{"t":"Automations — Personalisation tokens","b":"Drop tokens into any message to personalise it: Token Becomes {{contact.first_name}} Customer's first name {{contact.name}} · {{contact.email}} · {{contact.phone}} Other contact fields {{context.campaign_name}} Name of the campaign that fired the flow {{context.order_number}} · {{context.order_total}} Order details on order triggers {{context.cart_total}} · {{context.recovery_url}} Cart amount and checkout link {{context.tag_name}} The tag that was just added {{message.body}} The customer's inbound message"},{"t":"Automations — Popular recipes","b":"1. Welcome flow Trigger: New contact → Send WhatsApp: “Hi {{contact.first_name}}! 👋 Welcome to our store. Reply MENU to see the catalogue.” → Add tag: welcomed 2. Keyword menu Trigger: Message received (keywords: menu, price ) → Quick replies with buttons Pricing / Services / Talk to human → each button branches to its own message or Assign agent . 3. AI receptionist Trigger: Message received (no keywords) → Condition: contact has tag human_requested → if yes: Assign agent ; if no: AI reply . 4. Cart recovery Trigger: Cart abandoned → Wait 1 hour → “Your cart holds {{context.cart_total}} — finish here: {{context.recovery_url}}” → Wait 1 day → “Last chance! Coupon CART10 for 10% off.” 5. Post-campaign follow-up Trigger: Campaign sent → Add tag: received-offer → Wait 3 days → if the customer hasn't replied, send a gentle reminder with a coupon. ⚠️ Avoid loops Never let a “Tag added” automation add the same tag that triggers it — use a different tag name, or the flow will run forever."},{"t":"Automations — Webhook trigger","b":"Use Webhook received to start a flow from outside tools: 1 In the trigger panel, click Generate Token and copy your unique URL. 2 Point your website, CRM or payment gateway to POST that URL. 3 Include contact_id in the body when possible so the flow runs for that customer. ⚠️ Keep the URL secret Anyone with the token URL can trigger the flow. Regenerate the token if it leaks."},{"t":"Automations — Testing & monitoring","b":"Test button — preview the run without sending anything. Runs page — every execution is logged: which nodes ran, in what order, with what result. Open Automations → Runs . Real-world test — trigger the event for real (message yourself, add a test tag, POST a test webhook) and watch the run appear. 📎 Runs pending? Automation runs execute on a queue. If runs stay pending or an admin recently deployed, runs process within moments — contact support if runs never start."}]},{"file":"campaigns.html","title":"Campaigns","sections":[{"t":"Campaigns","b":"Send offers, updates and announcements to hundreds or thousands of contacts — guided by a wizard that keeps you compliant."},{"t":"Campaigns — The campaign wizard","b":"Open Broadcasting → Campaigns and click New Campaign . The wizard walks you through five steps: 1 Channel — pick WhatsApp, Messenger or Instagram. WhatsApp is the most common for broadcasts. 2 Audience — target contacts with filters: tags, segments, or all contacts. The wizard shows a live recipient count before you continue. 3 Content — write the message or pick an approved template and fill its variables. Add media (image, video, document) where the channel allows it. 4 Schedule — send immediately or pick a date and time. Scheduled campaigns run on their own; you can close the browser. 5 Review — check the summary (audience size, content, schedule) and launch. 💡 Warm up your sending New WhatsApp numbers should start with smaller broadcasts and engaged audiences — quality and limits grow with good engagement. Create the “Campaign sent” automation before launching if you want per-recipient follow-ups."},{"t":"Campaigns — Audience tips","b":"Use segments to keep reusable audiences — e.g. “VIP customers”, “Karachi leads”. Exclude recent non-deliveries by building segments on tags like undeliverable . Always honour opt-outs — add contacts who reply STOP to an opt-out tag and exclude it in campaigns."},{"t":"Campaigns — Tracking results","b":"Open a campaign to see its live stats — sent, delivered, read and replied counts — plus the per-recipient list. Compare campaigns over time in Reports → Campaigns . 📷 Screenshot placeholder: campaign report with delivered/read chart"},{"t":"Campaigns — SMS & email senders","b":"Campaigns can also go out over SMS and email once a sender is configured: Broadcasting → SMS Gateways — connect an SMS provider with guided, step-by-step setup screens. Broadcasting → Email Server — connect your SMTP with a built-in setup guide and test button."},{"t":"Campaigns — Common questions","b":"Can I send without a template? Only inside each customer's 24-hour reply window; outside it, WhatsApp requires an approved template. Can I cancel a scheduled campaign? Yes — open it before the send time and cancel from the campaign page. Why did some recipients not get it? Check the recipient list: invalid numbers, opt-outs and channel limits are the usual reasons."}]},{"file":"contacts.html","title":"Contacts & Leads","sections":[{"t":"Contacts & Leads","b":"Your audience database — import, organise, segment and find new leads to grow it."},{"t":"Contacts & Leads — The contacts list","b":"Open Contacts to see everyone in this workspace: name, phone, email, tags and last activity. Use the search bar and tag filters to narrow the list, and click any contact to open their full profile. The contact profile shows conversation history, tags, custom fields and notes — everything your team knows about this person in one screen."},{"t":"Contacts & Leads — Importing contacts","b":"1 Click Import on the contacts page. 2 Upload a CSV or Excel file . Include at least a phone number; name and email are recommended. 3 Map your file's columns to contact fields, and optionally tag everyone in this import (e.g. imported-march ). 4 Start the import. Large files process in the background — you'll see the count update as rows land. 💡 Duplicates Imports merge on matching phone numbers — a re-import updates existing contacts instead of duplicating them."},{"t":"Contacts & Leads — Tags","b":"Tags are free-form labels for filtering and automations: vip , wholesale , karachi , opted-out … Add or remove tags from a contact's profile, in bulk from the list, or automatically via automations . Tags power segments and campaign audiences — design a small set of consistent tags for your team."},{"t":"Contacts & Leads — Segments","b":"A segment is a saved, auto-updating filter — “all contacts tagged VIP with an email”, “leads from the last 30 days”. 1 Open Contacts → Segments and click New Segment . 2 Define conditions (tag exists, field equals, date ranges) and save with a clear name. 3 Use the segment as a campaign audience or to bulk-manage members. Members update automatically as contacts change."},{"t":"Contacts & Leads — Bulk actions","b":"Select multiple contacts (or filter first, then select all matches) to tag, untag or delete in one go. Bulk changes are ideal right after an import — tag the whole batch, then let segments and automations take over."},{"t":"Contacts & Leads — Lead finder","b":"Leads helps you discover new business contacts by location and business type, and save them as contacts to reach out to. 1 Open Leads from the sidebar. 2 Search by area and category (e.g. “DHA Lahore — dentists”). 3 Review results with names, addresses and phone numbers, then save the ones you want as contacts . ⚠️ Message responsibly Only message people who expect to hear from you. Unsolicited messages cause blocks — and blocks hurt your sender quality on every channel."}]},{"file":"ecommerce.html","title":"Ecommerce","sections":[{"t":"Ecommerce","b":"Connect your online store, sync products and orders, and message customers at every step — confirmation, shipping and abandoned carts."},{"t":"Ecommerce — Connecting a store","b":"1 Open Ecommerce → Stores and click Add Store . 2 Choose WooCommerce or Shopify and follow the connection steps (site URL & API credentials, or the Shopify connect flow). 3 Once connected, products and orders sync automatically — and customers found by phone or email link to their store records. 📎 What syncs Products (for sharing in chats), orders with line items and totals, and customers. Sync runs continuously in the background."},{"t":"Ecommerce — Products","b":"Under Ecommerce → Products you can browse the synced catalogue and share product cards right inside WhatsApp conversations — perfect for the inbox when a customer asks “do you have this in blue?”. In automations , the WooCommerce product and Shopify product nodes let a flow send a product card automatically, and the WhatsApp catalog node shares your catalog."},{"t":"Ecommerce — Orders","b":"Ecommerce → Orders lists every order with its status, items and customer. Open an order to see full details and jump to the customer's conversation. Order events power automations : order placed, fulfilled, cancelled and cart abandoned . Tokens like {{context.order_number}} , {{context.order_total}} and {{context.tracking_url}} personalise those messages."},{"t":"Ecommerce — Store automations","b":"From the Stores page, open WhatsApp Automations for one-click starter flows. Popular set-ups: Flow Trigger Typical message Order confirmation Order placed “Order {{context.order_number}} confirmed — total {{context.order_total}}. Thank you! 🙏” Shipping update Order fulfilled “Your order is on its way 🚚 Track: {{context.tracking_url}}” Win-back Order cancelled “Anything go wrong? Here's 15% off your next order: COMEBACK15” Cart recovery Cart abandoned “Your cart is waiting 🛒 Checkout: {{context.recovery_url}}” New customer welcome Customer created “Welcome! WELCOME10 gives you 10% off your first order 🎁” 💡 Recovery that works Send the first cart reminder about an hour after abandonment, and a final discount touch a day later — this sequence reliably outperforms a single blast."}]},{"file":"social-media.html","title":"Social Media","sections":[{"t":"Social Media","b":"Plan, create and schedule posts across your social networks from one composer — with AI help for ideas and captions."},{"t":"Social Media — Connecting accounts","b":"Under Social Media → Accounts , connect the pages and profiles you post to — Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, X (Twitter), YouTube and TikTok, depending on your plan. Each network uses its official login; connected accounts show their status right on the card."},{"t":"Social Media — The composer","b":"1 Open Social Media → Composer and pick the accounts to post to (one post can go to several networks at once). 2 Write the caption and attach media. A live preview shows exactly how the post will look on each network. 3 Publish now, or schedule it for the best time. Scheduled posts appear on the calendar and the posts list. 💡 Per-network tweaks The preview updates per selected network — trim captions to each platform's style before publishing instead of cross-posting blindly."},{"t":"Social Media — AI content planner","b":"Stuck for content? Open the AI planner from the posts page: Describe your business and pick the networks and tone. The planner drafts a batch of post ideas with captions you can accept into the composer. Edit anything before scheduling — AI drafts are starting points, not final copy."},{"t":"Social Media — Content calendar","b":"The calendar view shows all scheduled and published posts for the month, colour-coded by network. Drag or reschedule from the posts list, and filter by account to review one brand at a time. 📷 Screenshot placeholder: social content calendar month view"},{"t":"Social Media — Managing posts","b":"Social Media → Posts lists everything with status — draft, scheduled, publishing, published or failed. Open a post to edit drafts and scheduled items, or check the error message on failures (expired connections are the most common cause — reconnect the account and try again)."}]},{"file":"reports.html","title":"Reports","sections":[{"t":"Reports","b":"Five report views answer the big questions: how fast you reply, what campaigns achieve, what automations do, what AI costs you and how social performs."},{"t":"Reports — Inbox reports","b":"Reports → Inbox shows conversation health: Volume — inbound and outbound messages over time, per channel. Response times — how quickly your team replies (first reply and overall). Workload — conversations per agent and per status, so you can balance assignment. 💡 Use it weekly Watch first-response time as your north-star support metric — customers forgive slow resolutions more than slow first replies."},{"t":"Reports — Campaign reports","b":"Reports → Campaigns compares your broadcasts: delivery, read and reply rates per campaign, with trends across the period. Click into a campaign for its per-recipient detail (see Campaigns )."},{"t":"Reports — Automation reports","b":"Reports → Automations shows how many runs each automation executed and how they completed — successful runs, waits and failures. A sudden drop in runs usually means the automation got paused or its trigger stopped occurring."},{"t":"Reports — AI usage","b":"Reports → AI tracks chatbot activity: how many replies the AI generated over time and overall usage volume. Use it to watch adoption after launching a new chatbot or knowledge base."},{"t":"Reports — Social reports","b":"Reports → Social summarises your posting activity: posts per network, status breakdown and recent posts. Pair it with the content calendar to keep posting consistent."}]},{"file":"team-billing.html","title":"Team & Billing","sections":[{"t":"Team & Billing","b":"Bring your team on board with the right permissions, and manage your plan, payment methods and invoices."},{"t":"Team & Billing — Inviting teammates","b":"1 Open Account → Team (workspace administrators only) and click Invite . 2 Enter the person's email and role , then send the invite. 3 They receive an email invitation — accepting it creates their login and adds them to the workspace. Seats depend on your plan ; the Team page shows how many are in use."},{"t":"Team & Billing — Roles & permissions","b":"Role Can do Administrator Everything — billing, team, channels, settings and all messaging features Agent / Member Day-to-day work — inbox conversations, contacts, campaigns per assigned permissions Grant or restrict specific abilities per role (for example allow campaigns but hide billing) from the roles & permissions screen. Check the Audit Log to review who changed what."},{"t":"Team & Billing — Your subscription","b":"Account → Subscription shows your current plan, renewal date and usage against plan limits — channels, contacts, messages and more. Upgrade or downgrade any time; changes apply from the next billing cycle or immediately, depending on the change. 📎 Plan limits When you hit a limit (e.g. maximum connected channels), the app tells you which limit and offers an upgrade. Nothing breaks silently."},{"t":"Team & Billing — Choosing a plan","b":"Open Account → Plans to compare what each tier includes: number of workspaces, channels, contacts, message volume and team seats. Pick the tier that matches your current size — you can grow later."},{"t":"Team & Billing — Billing & invoices","b":"Account → Billing lists every charge with its date and amount. Open an invoice to view or print it (PDF via your browser's print dialog) for accounting. Update your payment method and billing details from the same page."}]},{"file":"settings.html","title":"Settings & Developer","sections":[{"t":"Settings & Developer","b":"Tune your workspace preferences, control notifications, export your data, and integrate with the API."},{"t":"Settings & Developer — Account settings","b":"Under Account → Settings you can: Update your profile — name, email, password and avatar. Set workspace defaults — language, currency and timezone used across the app. Manage workspaces if your plan includes more than one (see Workspaces )."},{"t":"Settings & Developer — Notifications","b":"Account → Notifications controls how the app gets your attention: Choose events worth interrupting for — new inbound message, assignment, campaign completion. Pick channels: in-app notifications and browser push (the first enable asks browser permission). Everything lands in the notifications inbox from the bell icon, regardless of settings."},{"t":"Settings & Developer — Data export","b":"Settings → Data Export generates downloadable copies of your workspace data — contacts and conversations — so you always own your information. Request an export and download the file when it's ready."},{"t":"Settings & Developer — Audit log","b":"The Audit Log records important changes made in your workspace: who changed settings, invited users, or modified automations, and when. Administrators can filter by user and action — invaluable when something “mysteriously” changed."},{"t":"Settings & Developer — Media library","b":"Developer → Media stores your uploaded images, videos, audio and documents in one place. Upload once and reuse the same file across campaigns, templates and automations — no re-uploading the same product photo every time."},{"t":"Settings & Developer — API tokens","b":"Integrate WhatsMine with your own systems through the API: 1 Open Developer → API Tokens and click New Token . 2 Name it after its purpose (e.g. “website-forms”) and create it. 3 Copy the token immediately — it's shown only once. Store it safely. 4 Send it as a bearer token with API requests. Revoke any token from the same page if it's no longer needed. ⚠️ Tokens are passwords Never commit tokens to public repositories or paste them in support chats. Revoke and re-create a token the moment you suspect exposure."},{"t":"Settings & Developer — Webhooks","b":"Developer → Webhooks pushes events from WhatsMine to your own endpoints — new message, contact created, order placed and more. 1 Add your endpoint URL and select the events to receive. 2 Save — events start POSTing to your URL as they happen. 3 Use the Deliveries view to inspect every attempt: payload, response code and retry state — this is where you debug a silent endpoint."},{"t":"Settings & Developer — API documentation","b":"Open Developer → API Docs for the full, in-app API reference — endpoints, parameters and examples using your own tokens. Developers should start there; this guide intentionally stays non-technical."}]},{"file":"faq.html","title":"FAQ & Troubleshooting","sections":[{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting","b":"Fast fixes for the questions we hear most. Click a question to expand the answer."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — Channels & connections","b":"My WhatsApp QR session disconnected. What do I do? Open Inbox → Channel Setup , find the disconnected session and re-scan the QR code with your phone ( WhatsApp → Linked Devices → Link a Device ). Sessions drop when the phone stays offline too long or the linked device is removed. Why can't my agent reply to this customer? Most likely the 24-hour window closed — free-form replies are only allowed within 24 hours of the customer's last message. Send an approved template message to re-open the conversation (Instagram allows tagged replies for up to 7 days). Instagram won't connect. Your Instagram account must be a Business or Creator (professional) account — personal accounts can't connect. Convert in the Instagram app under Settings, then retry the connection from Channel Setup."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — AI & chatbot","b":"The chatbot answers “contact our team” even though the info is in my knowledge base. Three usual causes: The document was edited but not re-indexed — re-save it in the KB. No embed-capable provider is configured — add one under AI → Providers, then re-index. The test question isn't literally covered by the KB text — bots answer from what's written, not what's implied. Add a clear Q&A for it. How do I stop the bot from answering completely? Deactivate the chatbot under AI → Chatbots . Once a customer has asked for a human (or an agent has replied), the bot stays out of that conversation. My microphone doesn't work for voice notes. The browser needs permission: click the lock icon in the address bar → Site settings → set Microphone to Allow , then reload the page. On Windows also check Settings → Privacy → Microphone if it still fails."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — Campaigns & messaging","b":"My campaign shows sent, but some contacts didn't receive it. Check the recipient list on the campaign page. Common reasons: invalid or changed phone numbers, contacts who opted out, template rejections, or channel messaging limits . Fix the numbers, re-import or re-send to the affected segment. Why was my template rejected? Meta reviews templates for category accuracy and spam-like content. Common rejections: marketing content marked as “utility”, excessive caps/emojis, or missing opt-out language. Revise and resubmit with honest categorisation (see templates )."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — Account & billing","b":"I hit a plan limit. What happens? The app shows which limit you reached (channels, contacts, seats…) and offers an upgrade. Your data is safe — nothing is deleted; you just can't add beyond the limit until you upgrade or free up space. How do I download invoices? Go to Account → Billing , open the invoice and print/save it as PDF from your browser. See Team & Billing . How do I delete my account or workspace data? Workspace administrators can export data first ( Settings → Data Export ), then contact support via Support → Tickets to close the account. We take data removal seriously and confirm once it's done."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — Still stuck?","b":"🎫 Open a support ticket From inside the app: Support → Tickets → New Ticket . Describe what you did, what you expected and what happened — screenshots help a lot, and tickets go straight to the team."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: My WhatsApp QR session disconnected. What do I do?","b":"Open Inbox → Channel Setup , find the disconnected session and re-scan the QR code with your phone ( WhatsApp → Linked Devices → Link a Device ). Sessions drop when the phone stays offline too long or the linked device is removed."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: Why can't my agent reply to this customer?","b":"Most likely the 24-hour window closed — free-form replies are only allowed within 24 hours of the customer's last message. Send an approved template message to re-open the conversation (Instagram allows tagged replies for up to 7 days)."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: Instagram won't connect.","b":"Your Instagram account must be a Business or Creator (professional) account — personal accounts can't connect. Convert in the Instagram app under Settings, then retry the connection from Channel Setup."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: The chatbot answers “contact our team” even though the info is in my knowledge base.","b":"Three usual causes: The document was edited but not re-indexed — re-save it in the KB. No embed-capable provider is configured — add one under AI → Providers, then re-index. The test question isn't literally covered by the KB text — bots answer from what's written, not what's implied. Add a clear Q&A for it."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: How do I stop the bot from answering completely?","b":"Deactivate the chatbot under AI → Chatbots . Once a customer has asked for a human (or an agent has replied), the bot stays out of that conversation."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: My microphone doesn't work for voice notes.","b":"The browser needs permission: click the lock icon in the address bar → Site settings → set Microphone to Allow , then reload the page. On Windows also check Settings → Privacy → Microphone if it still fails."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: My campaign shows sent, but some contacts didn't receive it.","b":"Check the recipient list on the campaign page. Common reasons: invalid or changed phone numbers, contacts who opted out, template rejections, or channel messaging limits . Fix the numbers, re-import or re-send to the affected segment."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: Why was my template rejected?","b":"Meta reviews templates for category accuracy and spam-like content. Common rejections: marketing content marked as “utility”, excessive caps/emojis, or missing opt-out language. Revise and resubmit with honest categorisation (see templates )."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: I hit a plan limit. What happens?","b":"The app shows which limit you reached (channels, contacts, seats…) and offers an upgrade. Your data is safe — nothing is deleted; you just can't add beyond the limit until you upgrade or free up space."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: How do I download invoices?","b":"Go to Account → Billing , open the invoice and print/save it as PDF from your browser. See Team & Billing ."},{"t":"FAQ & Troubleshooting — FAQ: How do I delete my account or workspace data?","b":"Workspace administrators can export data first ( Settings → Data Export ), then contact support via Support → Tickets to close the account. We take data removal seriously and confirm once it's done."}]}];
